"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 with a budget of $2M approved by the executive board. Key milestones include the successful completion of the design phase and the testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The team has expanded to include experts in machine learning and cloud computing, and Omar Jensen is leading the development phase. Future plans involve user interface enhancements starting in October, security protocol updates (including multi-factor authentication) effective January next year, and potential partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology. Feedback on the prototype is being sought from stakeholders by the end of November."
